# Template repository only — AI.CUSTOM.md is the per-repo DATA file,
# generated by AI/AI.canary.py --init (never shipped, never committed here).
# In customer repos AI.CUSTOM.md IS committed; this ignore is local to
# the template checkout and is not itself shipped. Regenerate on demand:
#   python3 AI/AI.canary.py --init --defaults
AI.CUSTOM.md

# AI.CONFLICTS.md is the per-repo conflict DISPOSITION file (decisions, not
# derivations), created by AI/AI.canary.py --init-conflicts. Same rule as
# AI.CUSTOM.md above: in customer repos it IS committed; here it must not be,
# because absence from the template is what stops a careless "cp AI.* target/"
# from clobbering a repo's recorded decisions.
AI.CONFLICTS.md

# AI.ENTERPRISE.md is generated by AI/AI.gen_enterprise.py from the installed-
# modules survey. It is per-repo production data, not a template file. If it
# appears here it was left from a test run and must not be committed.
AI.ENTERPRISE.md

# AI.STUDIO.md is per-repo data written by the AI from the studio_customization/
# export. Template repos have no Studio data; ignore it here to prevent a stray
# from being committed.
AI.STUDIO.md

# DOC.* files (DOC.CUSTOM.by.*.md, DOC.CONFLICTS.*.md, DOC.STUDIO.*.md) are
# generated derived docs that belong in customer repos (in AI/ after v13), not
# in the template repo. Ignore them here to prevent test-run junk accumulating.
DOC.*

# AI.PRODENV.*.md — per-category production environment files generated by
# AI/AI.gen_prodenv.py from a staging/production odoo-bin shell run. They are
# per-repo production data, not template files. In customer repos they ARE
# committed (the AI reads them for context); here they must not be, because the
# template has no production database to extract from.
# AI.PRODENV.MODULES.md is transient: consumed and deleted by AI.canary.py on
# the dev branch after the module list is applied to AI.CUSTOM.md.
AI.PRODENV.*.md
